## Changes

- `Default` now uses Java language code and allocates the next process-wide
  opaque ID, along with the existing Java-equivalent zero/null/default fields.
- Factory construction now uses the ID allocated by `Default`, so each command
  consumes one ID rather than allocating and discarding an extra ID.
- The JSON header regression now checks the Java default language code.
- The invoked Java fixture reflects the protected constructor and records the
  default fields and opaque-ID increment; Rust compares them in an isolated
  child process with serialization properties cleared.
- Fixture SHA-256:
  `b1dc81c3c70894dfd4e669a59027590bb6d79499a8c34e4c87ca1b6d60cb70ab`.

